cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "StereoGNN-BBB: protocol-controlled benchmarking of blood-brain barrier permeability models"
message: "If you use this benchmark, the corrected figures, or the leakage analysis, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Yasini-Ardekani
    given-names: Nabil
    orcid: ""
repository-code: "https://github.com/abinittio/StereoAwareGNN"
abstract: >-
  A stereochemistry-aware graph neural network for blood-brain barrier
  permeability prediction, benchmarked against seven alternative architectures
  (ChemBERTa, SMILES-CNN, SMILES-LSTM, ECFP+RF, ECFP+LogReg, descriptor MLP,
  ZINC-pretrained GNN) under random, scaffold and leakage-controlled external
  protocols. The study shows that evaluation protocol affects reported accuracy
  more than architecture choice: the best random-split model loses 0.21 AUC
  externally while a fingerprint random forest is nearly unaffected, and on
  novel chemistry every architecture approaches chance. Includes a documented
  retraction of a previously advertised 0.9612 external AUC that was produced
  under evaluation leakage.
keywords:
  - blood-brain barrier
  - graph neural networks
  - data leakage
  - model evaluation
  - cheminformatics
  - ADMET
license: MIT
